  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global energy districts programme - Colombia interventions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PLEASE READ UNTIL THE END OF THE BOX  The project &quot;Scaling up energy districts in Latin America and Caribbean region (ED3 LAC)&quot; has two main objectives:  1. Provide continuity to the promotion strategy for energy districts in Colombia and consolidate/complete the market transformation work that is currently being implemented by UNIDO in close collaboration with the Colombian government (Ministry of Environment and Sustainable Development (MADS) and Ministry of Energy and Mines (MEM)) within project 190085 funded by  the Swiss State Secretariat for Economic Affairs SECO.  2. Scaling up energy districts in the Latin America and Caribbean region as key innovative climate solution for energy transformation and decarbonization programmes of countries in the region, building on the unique experience, expertise, networks and knowledge assets accrued by UNIDO and its Colombian counterparts and partners.  Energy districts represent critically needed energy infrastructures for the energy efficient and decarbonisation development paths of cities and industries. Energy districts represent also one of the most successful examples of urban-industrial symbiosis. Energy districts generate multiple benefits, from climate to resources, to improved quality of health and job creation, contributing to several Sustainable Developmen</narrative>
  </description>
